## 🔢 Data Dictionary

### `city_light_pollution.csv`
| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| City, Country, Region | Text | Location identifiers |
| Latitude, Longitude | Decimal | Geographic coordinates |
| Year | Integer | Observation year (2018–2023) |
| Population_Million | Decimal | City population in millions |
| SQM_Value | Decimal | Sky Quality Meter reading (higher = darker sky; max ~22.0) |
| Bortle_Class | Integer | 1 (best) to 9 (worst) sky darkness classification |
| Artificial_Sky_Brightness_mcd_m2 | Decimal | Measured sky brightness in millicandela per m² |
| Visible_Stars_Count | Integer | Estimated naked-eye stars visible |
| Milky_Way_Visible | Text | Yes / Partial / No |
| Energy_Waste_GWh | Decimal | Estimated energy wasted on excess lighting |
| CO2_Emission_LightWaste_tons | Decimal | CO₂ equivalent from wasted light energy |
| Night_Sky_Quality_Score | Decimal | Normalized quality score (1–10) |
| Light_Pollution_Category | Text | Extreme / Severe / High / Moderate / Low |

### `wildlife_impact.csv`
| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Bird_Collision_Deaths_Annual | Integer | Annual bird building collision deaths |
| Sea_Turtle_Disorientation_Pct | Decimal | % of sea turtles disoriented by coastal light |
| Insect_Decline_Pct | Decimal | Estimated % insect population decline due to light |
| Bat_Activity_Reduction_Pct | Decimal | Reduction in bat foraging activity |
| Wildlife_Impact_Score | Decimal | Composite impact score (0–10) |

### `dark_sky_initiatives.csv`
| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| LED_Conversion_Pct | Decimal | % of street lights converted to LED |
| Curfew_Lighting_Hours | Integer | Hours per night with reduced lighting |
| Dark_Sky_Policy_Enacted | Text | Yes / No |
| Budget_Allocated_USD_Million | Decimal | Initiative budget in USD millions |
| Energy_Saved_GWh | Decimal | GWh saved through initiatives |
| SQM_Improvement | Decimal | Sky quality improvement achieved |
| Initiative_Status | Text | None / Planning / Active |

---

## 🔗 Data Model (Power BI Relationships)

```
city_light_pollution ──── bortle_scale_reference
        │  [Bortle_Class → Bortle_Class, Many-to-One]
        │
city_light_pollution ──── wildlife_impact
        │  [City+Year composite, via bridge or filtering]
        │
city_light_pollution ──── dark_sky_initiatives
           [City+Year composite, via bridge or filtering]
```

**Recommended approach**: Create a `City_Year` calculated column in each table (`= [City] & "|" & [Year]`) and use that as the relationship key.

---

## 📊 Dashboard Pages

### Page 1 — Sky Quality Overview
- KPI cards: Avg SQM, Avg Bortle Class, Visible Stars, % Cities without Milky Way
- Line chart: SQM trend by city (2018–2023)
- Horizontal bar chart: City pollution ranking by brightness
- Map visual: Bubble map with Bortle class color coding

### Page 2 — Wildlife & Ecological Impact
- Scatter plot: Light pollution rank vs. wildlife impact score
- Stacked column: Bird deaths by city
- Matrix: Insect decline % and bat activity reduction
- KPI: Annual bird collision deaths (global total)

### Page 3 — Dark Sky Initiatives
- Progress bars: LED conversion % by city
- Clustered bar: Energy saved vs. budget allocated
- Policy status donut: Active / Planning / None
- Timeline: SQM improvement trend for policy-active cities

### Page 4 — Scenario & What-If Analysis
- What-If slicer: LED Conversion Target (0–100%)
- Projected outcome cards: SQM, Energy Saved, Stars Recovered
- Dark Sky Health Index gauge (composite score)
- CO₂ savings projection by target LED %

---

## 🧮 Key DAX Measures

```dax
-- Composite Index (0–100)
[Dark Sky Health Index] =
VAR SQM_Weight   = DIVIDE([Avg SQM Score], 22) * 35
VAR Stars_Weight = DIVIDE([Avg Visible Stars], 4500) * 25
VAR Wildlife_W   = (10 - [Avg Wildlife Impact Score]) / 10 * 20
VAR Policy_W     = DIVIDE([Policy Adoption Rate Pct], 100) * 10
VAR LED_W        = DIVIDE([Avg LED Conversion Pct], 100) * 10
RETURN (SQM_Weight + Stars_Weight + Wildlife_W + Policy_W + LED_W) * 100

-- What-If Scenario
[Scenario SQM Projected] =
VAR TargetLED = 'LED_Conversion_Parm'[LED_Conversion_Parm Value]
VAR ImprovementPerPct = 0.015
RETURN [Avg SQM Score] + ((TargetLED - [Avg LED Conversion Pct]) * ImprovementPerPct)

-- Year-over-Year Sky Quality Change
[SQM YoY Change] =
VAR CY = MAX(city_light_pollution[Year])
VAR CV = CALCULATE([Avg SQM Score], city_light_pollution[Year] = CY)
VAR PV = CALCULATE([Avg SQM Score], city_light_pollution[Year] = CY - 1)
RETURN IF(NOT ISBLANK(PV), CV - PV, BLANK())
```

> Full DAX file with 45+ measures is in `/dax/all_measures.dax`

---

## 🚀 How to Run This Project

### Prerequisites
- Power BI Desktop (free download from Microsoft)
- Windows OS (required for Power BI Desktop)

### Steps

**1. Load data**
```
Open Power BI Desktop
→ Home → Get Data → Text/CSV
→ Load all 4 CSV files from /data/
```

**2. Build relationships (Model View)**
- Add `City_Year` calculated column in each table
- Connect: `city_light_pollution[City_Year]` → `wildlife_impact[City_Year]`
- Connect: `city_light_pollution[City_Year]` → `dark_sky_initiatives[City_Year]`
- Connect: `city_light_pollution[Bortle_Class]` → `bortle_scale_reference[Bortle_Class]`

**3. Create Date Table**
```dax
Date_Table = ADDCOLUMNS(
    GENERATESERIES(2018, 2023, 1),
    "Year", [Value],
    "Decade", IF([Value] < 2020, "2018–2019", "2020–2023")
)
```

**4. Add DAX measures**
- Open `/dax/all_measures.dax`
- Paste each measure into the relevant table using the Power BI DAX editor

**5. Create What-If parameter**
```
Modeling → New Parameter
Name: LED_Conversion_Parm
Data type: Decimal Number
Minimum: 0  |  Maximum: 100  |  Increment: 1  |  Default: 50
```

**6. Build dashboard pages**
- Follow the page layout in the "Dashboard Pages" section above
- Apply conditional formatting using the `[SQM Color HEX]` and `[Wildlife Color HEX]` measures

---

## 💡 Key Insights from the Data

1. **Dubai and Tokyo are the worst offenders** — sky brightness exceeding 5,800+ mcd/m², with only 26–31 stars visible vs. the 4,500 possible in a dark sky
2. **Reykjavik remains the benchmark** — SQM of 17.8–18.6, 4,250+ visible stars, with 97% LED conversion
3. **LED conversion ROI is strong** — cities with >60% LED conversion save an average of 630 GWh/year
4. **Bird deaths are massively underreported** — New York alone sees ~100,000 building collisions annually; this rises to 824,000 across the 13 study cities
5. **Policy lag is the main problem** — 5 of 13 cities still have no dark sky policy despite clear ROI data

---

## 📎 Data Sources & Methodology

| Dataset | Source |
|---|---|
| SQM / Sky Brightness | Globe at Night Citizen Science Program |
| Bortle Classification | International Dark-Sky Association (IDA) |
| Energy & CO₂ Estimates | IEA Lighting Market Report |
| Wildlife Data | IUCN Red List, Fatal Light Awareness Program (FLAP) |
| LED Conversion | City Government Sustainability Reports |

> **Note**: City-level granularity and multi-year trend data are modelled from real-world ranges and published benchmarks. Exact per-city values are indicative for portfolio demonstration purposes.

